<title>USA: BHC Q1 EPS $4.21 with $152.2 mln gain from UPN sale.</title>
<headline>BHC Q1 EPS $4.21 with $152.2 mln gain from UPN sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>BHC COMMUNICATIONS, INC.</p>
<p>		  Condensed Consolidated Statements of Income</p>
<p>		   Three Months Ended March 31, 1997 and 1996</p>
<p>		(Unaudited - In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>						    1997	    1996</p>
<p> Operating revenues		   $   101,118   $   101,045</p>
<p> Operating income			    17,492	  19,193</p>
<p>Other income (expense):</p>
<p>Gain on change of ownership</p>
<p>     in UPN, net			    152,224		--</p>
<p>  Interest and other income	     20,008	  22,482</p>
<p>Equity in United Paramount</p>
<p>     Network loss (a)		    (17,898)	(32,754)</p>
<p>						  154,334	(10,272)</p>
<p>Income before income taxes</p>
<p>	  and minority interest	   171,826	   8,921</p>
<p> Income tax provision			68,700	   4,300</p>
<p>Income before minority</p>
<p>	  interest			    103,126	   4,621</p>
<p> Minority interest (b)		    (3,636)	 (3,543)</p>
<p>	Net income			     99,490	   1,078</p>
<p> Avg shares outstanding(c)		 23,660	  24,188</p>
<p> Net income per share			  4.21	     .04</p>
<p>(a)  BHC owned all of United Paramount Network from its 1994 inception through January 15, when Viacom Inc exercised its option to acquire half of it. BHC continues to account for its interest in UPN under the equity method.</p>
<p>(b)  Reflects the interest of stockholders other than BHC in the operating results of United Television Inc., 59 percent owned at March 31.</p>
<p>(c)  The decline in average common shares outstanding reflects purchases by BHC of its Class A common shares.</p>
</text>
